# Input Rail — checks an incoming message for injection/off-topic content
# before the Agent Core ever sees it (CONTEXT.md's "Input Rail").
#
# This redefines NeMo's built-in `self check input` flow under its own name
# (harmless — Colang lets a project file override a library flow of the
# same name) purely so a reviewer opening this repo's rails config finds
# the Input Rail's actual logic here instead of needing to dig through
# NeMo's own library source. The behavior is unchanged from the library
# default: run the `self_check_input` action (an LLM call using the
# `self_check_input` prompt in ../config.yml), and if it says the message
# should be blocked, refuse and stop — the Agent Core is never invoked.
define flow self check input
  $allowed = execute self_check_input

  if not $allowed
    bot refuse to respond
    stop
